{"packet_id":"D009-01","doc_id":"D009","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance security deposit interest coverage","requirement":"Tenants in units covered by the ordinance, whether fully or partially covered, are entitled to interest on their security deposits. Tenants in exempt units are not.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Security deposit interest applies to units fully or partially covered by the ordinance, including partially covered units built after June 1980, most condominiums, homes with tenancies from 1996 on and certain subsidized units. Exempt units get no interest.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied duplex (Golden Duplex)","unit_limit":2}],"per_tenancy":"Exempt: a unit where the owner shares a kitchen or bath with the tenant; tenancies started after November 7, 2018 on properties where one unit is an ADU and either unit is owner-occupied.","coverage_quotes":["Single family homes with current tenancies that began before 1996** Fully Covered Yes Yes Yes Yes","Most condominiums** Partially Covered Yes No Yes Yes"]},"exemptions":"Golden Duplex (owner-occupied duplex); units where the owner shares a kitchen or bath with the tenant if the owner lived on the property when the tenancy started; ADU tenancies started after Nov 7, 2018 where either unit is owner-occupied; university dormitories; nonprofit cooperatives.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"Single family homes with current tenancies that began before 1996** Fully Covered Yes Yes Yes Yes","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
